IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa27-definitions`

-- coa27-ch4-register.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 Chapter 4 "The register of auditors etc"
-- (ss 1239, 1240), Chapter 4A (s 1240A) and Chapter 4B (s 1240B), lines 17518-17598 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- WHAT IS HERE AND WHAT IS NOT. These sections are mostly powers of the Secretary of State to make regulations
-- (ss 1239(4)-(6), (10), 1240(1)-(2), (4), 1240A(1)-(2), (4), 1240B): machinery, inert in the coverage table
-- (reason 2). What the text itself decides, and is encoded here: who goes on the register (s 1239(1)), what each
-- entry must contain (s 1239(2)-(3)), the Secretary of State's direction that the requirements do not apply
-- (s 1239(7)), how the obligations are enforced (s 1239(8)), and the definitions in ss 1239(9), 1240(3), 1240A(3).
--
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE the text says yes;
-- JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not decide (silent, list not closed,
-- includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording). A caller never turns NOTHING
-- into FALSE. Every name begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1239 The register of auditors
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The four kinds of firm that subsection (3) distinguishes.
DECLARE `s 1239(3) kind of firm` IS ONE OF
    `s 1239(3)(a) a body corporate other than a limited liability partnership`
    `s 1239(3)(b) a limited liability partnership`
    `s 1239(3)(c) a corporation sole`
    `s 1239(3)(d) a partnership`

DECLARE `s 1239 form of entrant` IS ONE OF
    `s 1239 an individual`
    `s 1239 a firm` HAS `s 1239 kind of firm` IS A `s 1239(3) kind of firm`

-- A person who is, or applies to be, on the register: the facts a witness can state about them.
DECLARE `s 1239 entrant` HAS
    `s 1239 form of the entrant` IS A `s 1239 form of entrant`
    `s 1239 eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1239 eligible by virtue of Chapter 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1239 a third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:17520 | (1) The Secretary of State must make regulations requiring the keeping of a register of—
-- src:17521 | (a) the persons eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, and
-- src:17522 | (b) third country auditors (see Chapter 5) who apply to be registered in the specified manner and in relation to whom specified requirements are met.
@ref s 1239(1) The register of auditors: who is on it (src:17520-17522)
GIVEN e IS A `s 1239 entrant`
      `the third country auditor applies to be registered in the specified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `specified requirements are met in relation to the third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1239(1) the person is to be entered in the register` MEANS
    IF e's `s 1239 eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (a) the persons eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor
    ELSE IF e's `s 1239 a third country auditor`
              AND `the third country auditor applies to be registered in the specified manner`
              AND `specified requirements are met in relation to the third country auditor`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- (b) third country auditors who apply ... and in relation to whom specified requirements are met
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) third country auditors (see Chapter 5) who apply to be registered in the specified manner and in relation to whom specified requirements are met"

-- What the regulations must require each entry to contain (subsection (2)); the text itself says "and may require
-- each person's entry to contain other specified information".
DECLARE `s 1239(2) required item` IS ONE OF
    `s 1239(2)(a) his name and address`
    `s 1239(2)(b) the specified information relating to any firm on whose behalf the individual is responsible for statutory audit work`
    `s 1239(2)(c) the specified information relating to the individuals responsible for statutory audit work on the firm's behalf`
    `s 1239(2)(d) the name of the relevant supervisory body`
    `s 1239(2)(e) the information mentioned in subsection (3)`
    `s 1239(2)(f) the name and address of each owner or shareholder of the firm and of each member of its administrative or management body`

-- src:17523 | (2) The regulations must require each person's entry in the register to contain—
-- src:17524 | (a) his name and address,
-- src:17525 | (b) in the case of an individual eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, the specified information relating to any firm on whose behalf he is responsible for statutory audit work,
-- src:17526 | (c) in the case of a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, the specified information relating to the individuals responsible for statutory audit work on its behalf,
-- src:17527 | (d) in the case of an individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2, the name of the relevant supervisory body, . . .
-- src:17528 | (e) in the case of a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2 . . . , the information mentioned in subsection (3), and
-- src:17529 | (f) in the case of a third country auditor which is a firm, the name and address of each person who is—
-- src:17530 | (i) an owner or shareholder of the firm, or
-- src:17531 | (ii) a member of the firm's administrative or management body.
-- src:17532 | and may require each person's entry to contain other specified information.
@ref s 1239(2) The register of auditors: what an entry must contain (src:17523-17532)
GIVEN e IS A `s 1239 entrant`
      item IS A `s 1239(2) required item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1239(2) the regulations must require the entry to contain` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 1239(2)(a) his name and address` THEN JUST TRUE -- "each person's entry"
    WHEN `s 1239(2)(b) the specified information relating to any firm on whose behalf the individual is responsible for statutory audit work` THEN
        CONSIDER e's `s 1239 form of the entrant`
        WHEN `s 1239 an individual` THEN
            IF e's `s 1239 eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of an individual eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor"
        WHEN `s 1239 a firm` k THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of an individual"
    WHEN `s 1239(2)(c) the specified information relating to the individuals responsible for statutory audit work on the firm's behalf` THEN
        CONSIDER e's `s 1239 form of the entrant`
        WHEN `s 1239 a firm` k THEN
            IF e's `s 1239 eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) in the case of a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor"
        WHEN `s 1239 an individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) in the case of a firm"
    WHEN `s 1239(2)(d) the name of the relevant supervisory body` THEN
        IF e's `s 1239 eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` AND e's `s 1239 eligible by virtue of Chapter 2`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) in the case of an individual or firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2"
    WHEN `s 1239(2)(e) the information mentioned in subsection (3)` THEN
        CONSIDER e's `s 1239 form of the entrant`
        WHEN `s 1239 a firm` k THEN
            IF e's `s 1239 eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` AND e's `s 1239 eligible by virtue of Chapter 2`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) in the case of a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor by virtue of Chapter 2"
        WHEN `s 1239 an individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) in the case of a firm"
    WHEN `s 1239(2)(f) the name and address of each owner or shareholder of the firm and of each member of its administrative or management body` THEN
        CONSIDER e's `s 1239 form of the entrant`
        WHEN `s 1239 a firm` k THEN
            IF e's `s 1239 a third country auditor`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(f) in the case of a third country auditor which is a firm"
        WHEN `s 1239 an individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(f) in the case of a third country auditor which is a firm"

DECLARE `s 1239(3) required information` IS ONE OF
    `s 1239(3)(a) the name and address of each person who is a director of the body or holds any shares in it`
    `s 1239(3)(b) the name and address of each member of the partnership`
    `s 1239(3)(c) the name and address of the individual for the time being holding the office by the name of which he is the corporation sole`
    `s 1239(3)(d) the name and address of each partner`

-- src:17533 | (3) The information referred to in subsection (2)(e) is—
-- src:17534 | (a) in relation to a body corporate, except where paragraph (b) applies, the name and address of each person who is a director of the body or holds any shares in it;
-- src:17535 | (b) in relation to a limited liability partnership, the name and address of each member of the partnership;
-- src:17536 | (c) in relation to a corporation sole, the name and address of the individual for the time being holding the office by the name of which he is the corporation sole;
-- src:17537 | (d) in relation to a partnership, the name and address of each partner.
@ref s 1239(3) The register of auditors: the information in subsection (2)(e) (src:17533-17537)
GIVEN k IS A `s 1239(3) kind of firm`
GIVETH A `s 1239(3) required information`
`s 1239(3) the information referred to in subsection (2)(e) for a` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `s 1239(3)(a) a body corporate other than a limited liability partnership` THEN `s 1239(3)(a) the name and address of each person who is a director of the body or holds any shares in it`
    WHEN `s 1239(3)(b) a limited liability partnership` THEN `s 1239(3)(b) the name and address of each member of the partnership`
    WHEN `s 1239(3)(c) a corporation sole` THEN `s 1239(3)(c) the name and address of the individual for the time being holding the office by the name of which he is the corporation sole`
    WHEN `s 1239(3)(d) a partnership` THEN `s 1239(3)(d) the name and address of each partner`

-- src:17551 | (7) The Secretary of State may direct in writing that the requirements imposed by the regulations . . . , or such of those requirements as are specified in the direction, are not to apply, in whole or in part, in relation to a particular registered third country auditor or class of registered third country auditors.
@ref s 1239(7) The register of auditors: direction that requirements do not apply (src:17551-17551)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has directed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction covers this registered third country auditor, or a class of registered third country auditors that includes it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction covers the requirement in question (the direction applies in whole, or the requirement is one specified in it)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1239(7) the requirements imposed by the regulations apply to the registered third country auditor` MEANS
    IF       `the Secretary of State has directed in writing`
         AND `the direction covers this registered third country auditor, or a class of registered third country auditors that includes it`
         AND `the direction covers the requirement in question (the direction applies in whole, or the requirement is one specified in it)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not to apply, in whole or in part"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): without a direction the regulations say what applies

-- "an injunction or, in Scotland, an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988": the remedy that
-- subsection (8) here, s 1249(3) and s 1254(3) all name. Declared once, here, and used by those sections.
DECLARE `s 1239(8) remedy` IS ONE OF
    `s 1239(8) an injunction`
    `s 1239(8) an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988`

-- src:17552 | (8) The obligations imposed by regulations under this section on such persons as are mentioned in subsection (5)(b) or (e) are enforceable on the application of the Secretary of State by injunction or, in Scotland, by an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988 (c. 36).
@ref s 1239(8) The register of auditors: enforcement of obligations (src:17552-17552)
GIVEN `the obligation is imposed by regulations under this section on a body designated by order under section 1252 (subsection (5)(b)) or on a person within subsection (5)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1239(8) remedy`
`s 1239(8) the obligation is enforceable by` MEANS
    IF `the obligation is imposed by regulations under this section on a body designated by order under section 1252 (subsection (5)(b)) or on a person within subsection (5)(e)`
       AND `the Secretary of State has applied`
    THEN
        IF `the proceedings are in Scotland`
        THEN JUST `s 1239(8) an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988`
        ELSE JUST `s 1239(8) an injunction`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The obligations imposed by regulations under this section on such persons as are mentioned in subsection (5)(b) or (e) are enforceable on the application of the Secretary of State"

-- src:17553 | (9) In this section “specified” means specified by regulations under this section.
@ref s 1239(9) The register of auditors: "specified" (src:17553-17553)
GIVEN `the matter is specified by regulations under section 1239` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1239(9) the matter is specified` MEANS
    IF `the matter is specified by regulations under section 1239`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified by regulations under this section"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1240 Information to be made available to public
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17564 | (3) In this section “specified” means specified by regulations under this section.
@ref s 1240(3) Information to be made available to public: "specified" (src:17564-17564)
GIVEN `the matter is specified by regulations under section 1240` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1240(3) the matter is specified` MEANS
    IF `the matter is specified by regulations under section 1240`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified by regulations under this section"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1240A Power to approve third countries as equivalent or transitional third countries
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17582 | (3) In this section, “audit regulatory regime” in relation to a country or territory, means the system of public oversight, quality assurance, investigations and sanctions for auditors in that country or territory.
@ref s 1240A(3) Power to approve third countries: "audit regulatory regime" (src:17582-17582)
GIVEN `the country or territory has a system of public oversight of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the country or territory has a system of quality assurance for auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the country or territory has a system of investigations of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the country or territory has a system of sanctions for auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1240A(3) the system is an audit regulatory regime` MEANS
    IF       `the country or territory has a system of public oversight of auditors`
         AND `the country or territory has a system of quality assurance for auditors`
         AND `the country or territory has a system of investigations of auditors`
         AND `the country or territory has a system of sanctions for auditors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“audit regulatory regime” in relation to a country or territory, means the system of public oversight, quality assurance, investigations and sanctions for auditors"
